# ⚠️ WORKFLOW DISABLED — retained only as a reference copy.
#
# This file is intentionally inert:
#   * It has no `on:` trigger, so GitHub Actions NEVER schedules it.
#   * The live `android-release.yml` was removed from .github/workflows/.
#
# Why it is disabled
#   Stale, broken duplicate of the working `.github/workflows/release.yml`.
#   Both are named "Android Release (APK + AAB)" and both trigger on the same
#   `v*` tag push, producing two overlapping runs. This one also:
#     * built outdated, un-flavored Gradle targets `assembleRelease`/
#       `bundleRelease`, which no longer exist once product flavors (prod/e2e)
#       were added — a guaranteed "Build release APK + AAB" failure;
#     * used Node 18 while the app requires Node 22 (its "Install JS
#       dependencies" step was the first thing to fail at v1.18.1);
#     * skipped the .env / google-services.json setup the real build now
#       requires, and used non-flavored output paths (app-release.apk /
#       app-release.aab instead of app-prod-release.apk/-aab).
#
# The single source of truth for the APK + AAB release is
#   .github/workflows/release.yml
# Resurrect a second Android workflow by adapting release.yml, not this file.
